From a80b0de184f0f77cc578ab51cc91cfae0026dc6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zhongteng Gui <dragon-archer@outlook.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:56:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] mingw: Remove outdated /mingw stuff from FLAGS_FOR_TARGET
 [PR126608]

/mingw is only used by MSYS 1, which has been obsolete for a long time.
The current users of target *-w64-mingw32 either uses their own prefix
(MSYS2 and its derivatives, w64devkit, etc.), or use the default prefix
/usr (Cross-compiling on linux, e.g. Conda-forge).

More cleanups of /mingw may be done in future patches.

ChangeLog:

	PR target/126608
	* configure.ac (x86_64-*mingw* | *-w64-mingw*): Do not use
	/mingw symlink.
	* configure: Regenerate.

Signed-off-by: Zhongteng Gui <dragon-archer@outlook.com>
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Yong <10walls@gmail.com>
---
 configure    | 4 +---
 configure.ac | 4 +---
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/configure b/configure
index 07f62a81bb9..6ee5071c58b 100755
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -11883,9 +11883,7 @@ esac
 
 case "$target" in
   x86_64-*mingw* | *-w64-mingw*)
-  # MinGW-w64 does not use newlib, nor does it use winsup. It may,
-  # however, use a symlink named 'mingw' in ${prefix} .
-    FLAGS_FOR_TARGET=$FLAGS_FOR_TARGET' -L${prefix}/${target}/lib -L${prefix}/mingw/lib -isystem ${prefix}/${target}/include -isystem ${prefix}/mingw/include'
+  # MinGW-w64 does not use newlib, nor does it use winsup. No special flags needed.
     ;;
   *-mingw*)
   # MinGW can't be handled as Cygwin above since it does not use newlib.
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
index cb5c4271090..f128d838f16 100644
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -3944,9 +3944,7 @@ esac
 
 case "$target" in
   x86_64-*mingw* | *-w64-mingw*)
-  # MinGW-w64 does not use newlib, nor does it use winsup. It may,
-  # however, use a symlink named 'mingw' in ${prefix} .
-    FLAGS_FOR_TARGET=$FLAGS_FOR_TARGET' -L${prefix}/${target}/lib -L${prefix}/mingw/lib -isystem ${prefix}/${target}/include -isystem ${prefix}/mingw/include'
+  # MinGW-w64 does not use newlib, nor does it use winsup. No special flags needed.
     ;;
   *-mingw*)
   # MinGW can't be handled as Cygwin above since it does not use newlib.
